<Component>
<Description>
An ideal Capacitor 
[value] is the capacity in Farad
[inivolt] is the initial voltage in Volt
   (Warning: Depending on the ngspice version, an initial condition may not work but be set to zero.
    Since this is an internal problem in spice and also appears in other applications than CNS (also found in
    qucs 0.0.21) the CNS can not solve this problem from spice. You might want to simulate the initial value by an external current source instead.)
[smbl] is the symbol type. but ignored, because symbol is defined in Symbol section
</Description>
<qucs_sch>
C [name] [active] [xpos] [ypos] [xtext] [ytext] [mirrorx] [rotate] [value] [value_v] [inivolt] [inivolt_v] [smbl] [smbl_v]
</qucs_sch>
<eeschema_sch>
    L pspice:CAP
</eeschema_sch>
<eeschema_sch>
    L Device:C
    ALIAS Device:C_Small Device:CP Device:CP_Small Device:CP1 Device:CP1_Small
</eeschema_sch>
<eeschema_sch>
    L Device:CTRIM
    ALIAS Device:CTRIM_Small
</eeschema_sch>
<eeschema_sch>
    L Device:C_Variable
</eeschema_sch>
<Spice>
    DEFINE [farad] AS_NUMBER OF:[value]
    IF [inivolt] THEN DEFINE [inivolt] AS_NUMBER OF:[inivolt]ENDIF 
	IF [farad] THEN
        DEFINE [value] AS_NULL
    ELSE
        DEFINE [farad] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:farad IN:[value]
        DEFINE [farad] AS_NUMBER OF:[farad]
        DEFINE [inivolt] AS_WORD_RIGHT OF:inivolt IN:[value]
        DEFINE [inivolt] AS_NUMBER OF:[inivolt]
    ENDIF
    IF ![farad] THEN
        <Dialog title="missing Farad value for [name]" type="error" dimension="450x150"> 
            The capacitor named [name] at ([xpos] | [ypos]) has an invalid value, "[value]".
            This component expects an C value in Farad. 
            Please enter a number at that place.
        </Dialog>
    ENDIF
    C_[name] [pin1] [pin2] [farad] IF[inivolt]THENic=[inivolt]ENDIF
</Spice>
